      "content": "**Immediately** stop whatever you are doing and treat that battery like a high-risk, potentially volatile situation. Do not puncture, crush, or attempt to charge it; the swelling itself is a major warning sign of internal chemical instability. You must handle it with extreme care, perhaps with the protective gloves you use for handling volatile materials, and keep it away from any sparks or heat sources.\n\nFor safe disposal, you absolutely cannot just toss it in the regular trash. You need to take it to a dedicated hazardous waste collection site or a specialized electronics recycling program. These facilities are equipped to handle lithium-ion batteries safely, preventing the kind of fire hazard that could be caused by improper disposal. Always check with your local municipal waste management to find the nearest designated drop-off point.",
