      "content": "The erratic behavior you're seeing is a classic symptom of internal gas buildup due to chemical degradation inside the battery cells. These batteries aren't exhibiting a \"mind of their own,\" but rather a runaway chemical reaction, which is why they can become so unpredictable. As the internal structure breaks down, gases build up, causing the casing to swell, and this instability increases the risk of thermal runaway—a rapid, uncontrollable increase in temperature.\n\nIt's a dangerous situation, and the level of danger is high because the failure mechanism is internal and hard to predict. You should treat every moment it is in your possession as if a fire is imminent, which is why professional disposal is the only true solution. Keep it isolated, away from anything that could trigger a short or heat, until the proper hazardous waste handlers take it.",
